From: GMagisk9527 <GMagisk9527@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: ufs-qcom: do not enable test bus at init

[ Found in OnePlus 6.1.141 OKI source ]

ufs_qcom_init() always programs UNIPRO testbus 37 and sets
TEST_BUS_EN / UFS_REG_TEST_BUS_EN. That muxes debug hardware and
keeps extra clocks/logic alive. Dump paths can still call
ufs_qcom_testbus_config() later.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index 3b13449..cee0474 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -1034,12 +1034,11 @@ static int ufs_qcom_init(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	if (hba->dev->id < MAX_UFS_QCOM_HOSTS)
 		ufs_qcom_hosts[hba->dev->id] = host;
 
+	/*
+	 * Test bus mux clocks debug hardware. Keep it off unless a
+	 * subsequent dump/sysfs path calls ufs_qcom_testbus_config().
+	 */
 	ufs_qcom_get_default_testbus_cfg(host);
-	err = ufs_qcom_testbus_config(host);
-	if (err)
-		/* Failure is non-fatal */
-		dev_warn(dev, "%s: failed to configure the testbus %d\n",
-				__func__, err);
 
 	return 0;
 
